# Layrus Labs — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development (git-ignored), and set the same names in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for production. Nothing here is
# needed to build or serve the site; only the assistant reads them.

# ── The assistant ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a key the chat route answers 503 with a message rather than failing
# in a way nobody can read.

# One provider: DeepSeek, via its OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint.
# Get a key at https://platform.deepseek.com
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# Which model. Defaults to deepseek-chat; deepseek-reasoner also works, but it
# streams its reasoning first, which the route drops.
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# Only needed if you point at a proxy or a different region.
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com

# ── Spend control ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set a monthly limit on the provider's own dashboard — that is the only real
# ceiling on this endpoint. The route's rate limit is per-instance and
# best-effort; see the note in app/api/chat/route.ts.

# ── Chat transcripts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Neon Postgres database. Create one (Vercel → Storage → Neon, or
# neon.tech), then run scripts/schema.sql against it once.
#
# Without this the chat still works; transcripts are simply not stored.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require

# ── Enquiry notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spacemail has no sending API; these are the mailbox's own SMTP
# credentials, from Spacemail Manager -> mailbox -> IMAP/POP3/SMTP.
#
# The answer "no credentials" is not an error: enquiries are stored in the
# database either way, they are just not emailed to you.
# SMTP_HOST=mail.spacemail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=hello@layrus.com
# SMTP_PASS=<the mailbox password>
# ENQUIRY_TO=hello@layrus.com
#
# Optional. Sending as a subaddress keeps form mail filterable in the inbox,
# with replies still going to the enquirer via replyTo. It must be created as
# an alias on this mailbox first, or the server will refuse to send as it.
# Defaults to SMTP_USER when unset.
# SMTP_FROM=website@layrus.com
